p.src:
At the end of the blackboard calculation, replace the plus sign by a minus: $\ket{\psi_-}
  =
  \frac{1}{\sqrt2}
  \left(\ket{ud}-\ket{du}\right).$ The change leaves the local expectations in Equation [eq:l04-zero-local-spin] equal to zero and leaves the third-axis outcomes opposite. It does change the transverse joint correlations. This minus-sign state is the spin singlet, the rotationally invariant state in which the two spins are opposite along every common measurement axis.

